]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§22.10’s handler is ONE function from an event to one answer, which is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right shape for the wire and the wrong shape for the code. A reactor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered for three events opens with a "},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"event.event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"switch is where two defects live. The first is cheap: a misspelled event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binds nothing and is discovered as an event that never fires. The second is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not — it is the "},{"code":"default:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" arm that returns "},{"code":".allow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on behalf of code that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never ran, which is §22.10 rule 2’s defect relocated into user code where the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rule does not reach it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"A BUILDER RATHER THAN AN ATTRIBUTE","type":"text"}]},{"text":", and §22.14 records why: a Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reactor handler is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure, and collecting ","type":"text"},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" members by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reflection costs a runtime dependency an SDK should not add to hand out an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute. A builder type-checks the closure against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"(ReactorEvent) async throws -> ReactorAnswer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" at compile time, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stricter than what the reflection would have bought. Kotlin made the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trade for the same reason.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"PURE SUGAR.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" It opens no connection, consumes no queue, verifies no event,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signs no reply and interprets no ","type":"text"},{"code":"timeout_ms","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; its output is exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler the runtime accepts (rule 1).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/reactorServe(config:transport:handler:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/reactorServe(config:transport:handler:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reactorServe","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"config"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK13ReactorConfigV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ReactorConfig"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"transport","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK16ReactorTransportP","text":"ReactorTransport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"handler","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK12ReactorEventV","text":"ReactorEvent","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK13ReactorAnswera","text